    "Syllabus references, scope and level of difficulty are to be checked against the official text; all facts, formulas and worked examples to be verified by a teacher before release."
   ],
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "methode",
     "title": "Implicit differentiation",
     "md": "When $y$ cannot be isolated, differentiate every term with respect to $x$. A term in $y$ needs the chain rule: $\\frac{d}{dx}(y^2)=2y\\frac{dy}{dx}$ and $\\frac{d}{dx}(xy)=y+x\\frac{dy}{dx}$. Then collect the $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ terms and solve."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "formule",
     "title": "Parametric curves",
     "md": "If $x=f(t)$ and $y=g(t)$ then $\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{dy/dt}{dx/dt}$. The point at a given $t$ is found by substituting into both. Eliminate $t$ to get the Cartesian equation when possible, e.g. $x=3\\cos t$, $y=2\\sin t$ gives $\\frac{x^2}{9}+\\frac{y^2}{4}=1$."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "pieges",
     "title": "Common mistakes",
     "md": "Forgetting $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ when differentiating a $y$ term. For parametric curves $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ is NOT $\\frac{dx}{dy}$ upside down by accident: divide $\\frac{dy}{dt}$ by $\\frac{dx}{dt}$, in that order."
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 1",
     "statement": "Find the gradient of $x^2+xy+y^2=7$ at $(1,2)$, after checking the point lies on the curve.",
     "steps": [
      "$1+2+4=7$, so the point is on the curve.",
      "Differentiate: $2x+y+x\\frac{dy}{dx}+2y\\frac{dy}{dx}=0$, so $\\frac{dy}{dx}=-\\frac{2x+y}{x+2y}$.",
      "At $(1,2)$: $-\\frac{4}{5}$."
     ],
     "answer": "Gradient $-\\frac{4}{5}$"
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 2",
     "statement": "A curve has $x=t^2$, $y=2t$. Find $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ and the tangent at $t=2$.",
     "steps": [
      "$\\frac{dy}{dt}=2$, $\\frac{dx}{dt}=2t$, so $\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac1t$.",
      "At $t=2$: point $(4,4)$, gradient $\\frac{1}{2}$; tangent $y-4=\\frac{1}{2}(x-4)$, i.e. $y=\\frac{x}{2}+2$."
     ],
     "answer": "$\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{1}{t}$; tangent $y=\\frac{x}{2}+2$",
