  {
   "id": "gceal-maths-trig-formulae",
   "title": "Compound angles, double angles and the R-form",
   "minutes": 25,
   "programRef": "Cameroon GCE Board — Advanced Level Mathematics, Pure Mathematics (Upper Sixth part; to be checked against the official syllabus)",
   "status": "draft",
   "author": "CastBridge (AI draft)",
   "source": "Original writing following the Cameroonian curriculum; to be reviewed by a teacher",
   "objectives": [
    "Use addition and double-angle formulae",
    "Write $a\\sin x+b\\cos x$ as $R\\sin(x+\\alpha)$",
    "Solve equations and prove identities"
   ],
   "prerequisites": [],
   "exercises": [
    "gceal-maths-differentiation-e19",
    "gceal-maths-differentiation-e20",
    "gceal-maths-differentiation-e21",
    "gceal-maths-differentiation-e22",
    "gceal-maths-differentiation-e23",
    "gceal-maths-differentiation-e24"
   ],
   "selfCheck": [
    "gceal-maths-trig-formulae-q1",
    "gceal-maths-trig-formulae-q2",
    "gceal-maths-trig-formulae-q3",
    "gceal-maths-trig-formulae-q4",
    "gceal-maths-trig-formulae-q5"
   ],
   "reviewNotes": [
    "Half-angle (t) formulae and factor formulae not covered.",
    "Syllabus references, scope and level of difficulty are to be checked against the official text; all facts, formulas and worked examples to be verified by a teacher before release."
   ],
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "formule",
     "title": "Addition formulae",
     "md": "$\\sin(A\\pm B)=\\sin A\\cos B\\pm\\cos A\\sin B$; $\\cos(A\\pm B)=\\cos A\\cos B\\mp\\sin A\\sin B$; $\\tan(A\\pm B)=\\frac{\\tan A\\pm\\tan B}{1\\mp\\tan A\\tan B}$. Note the sign flip in the cosine formula."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "formule",
     "title": "Double-angle formulae",
     "md": "$\\sin2A=2\\sin A\\cos A$; $\\cos2A=\\cos^2A-\\sin^2A=2\\cos^2A-1=1-2\\sin^2A$; $\\tan2A=\\frac{2\\tan A}{1-\\tan^2A}$. Choose the form of $\\cos2A$ that leaves a single trig function."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "methode",
     "title": "The R-form",
     "md": "$a\\sin x+b\\cos x=R\\sin(x+\\alpha)$ with $R=\\sqrt{a^2+b^2}$, $\\tan\\alpha=\\frac ba$ ($a,b>0$, $\\alpha$ acute). The maximum value is $R$ and the minimum $-R$. To solve $a\\sin x+b\\cos x=c$: solve $\\sin(x+\\alpha)=\\frac cR$, then subtract $\\alpha$."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "pieges",
     "title": "Common mistakes",
     "md": "$\\sin(A+B)\\neq\\sin A+\\sin B$. $\\cos2A\\neq2\\cos A$. When solving $\\sin(x+\\alpha)=k$ list solutions for $x+\\alpha$ over the SHIFTED interval before subtracting $\\alpha$."
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 1",
     "statement": "Find the exact value of $\\sin75\\degree$.",
     "steps": [
      "$\\sin75\\degree=\\sin(45\\degree+30\\degree)=\\sin45\\cos30+\\cos45\\sin30$.",
      "$=\\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}\\cdot\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{\\sqrt6+\\sqrt2}{4}$."
     ],
     "answer": "$\\frac{\\sqrt6+\\sqrt2}{4}\\approx0.966$"
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 2",
